 The shared CLI is `audiocompose bundle compose NAME.ssmd-bundle`; `--variant VARIANT` targets one variant, while omitting it enables state-aware batch composition. Books support chapter selection and documents accept only `all`. The `--save-audiojobs` option is a root directory for both kinds; in batch mode each selected variant receives a namespaced `DIR/<variant>` subdirectory. Workspace-derived defaults resolve `renderplan/<variant>`, `voicerender/<variant>`, and `audiocompose/<variant>` beneath the supplied root.

-`list_bundle_variants()` is the read-only source of variant discovery and pipeline readiness. `compose_bundle_batch()` selects valid variants with `ready_to_compose` and open composition work (or, with batch `--force`, all valid compose-ready variants including complete ones), then calls `compose_bundle()` once per selected variant. It forwards force unchanged so existing output-ownership/provenance checks remain authoritative, isolates failures unless fail-fast is requested, and re-lists artifacts to derive final status. This is orchestration only: there is no persistent batch-state database and no duplicate book/document composition logic.
+`list_bundle_variants()` remains the read-only source of global, whole-variant discovery and pipeline status; a transient chapter selector never changes its meaning. `compose_bundle_batch()` uses an internal operation-scoped inspection for book selectors, validating only the selected RenderPlans and VoiceRender artifacts while retaining all authoritative chapter IDs for report ownership checks. The requested selection scopes readiness, compose status, scheduling, counters, and final relisting; omitted selectors and `--chapters all` retain whole-variant behavior. Documents keep their existing single-document semantics. Batch composition selects valid, compose-ready variants with open composition work (or, with batch `--force`, all valid compose-ready variants including complete ones), then calls `compose_bundle()` once per selected variant. It forwards force unchanged so existing output-ownership/provenance checks remain authoritative, isolates failures unless fail-fast is requested, and re-inspects artifacts using the same operation scope to derive final status. This is orchestration only: there is no persistent batch-state database and no duplicate book/document composition logic.
 Composition policies, output verification, provenance-based reuse, force behavior, failure handling, and progress callbacks are delegated to their existing kind-specific services. CLI JSON is wrapped in a neutral bundle result; persistent internal report formats are unchanged.

 An AudioJob is an ordered collection of `AudioClip` and `Silence` items. A clip references either an in-memory NumPy `AudioBufferSource` or a file-backed `AudioFileSource`, followed by ordered numeric operations allowed by its schema version. V1 contains the existing static operations; v2 adds the generic time-varying `RatePitchEnvelope`. Clip anchors and spans are generic timing metadata. Output policy contains the final sample rate, channel count, clipping behavior, and complete-output loudness policy.
